### [152. Maximum Product Subarray](https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-product-subarray/)
- Solved using prefix and suffix products to handle negative numbers and zeros.
- Maintained running products from both ends to ensure maximum subarray product is captured.

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    int maxProduct(vector<int>& nums) {
        int pre = 1, suf = 1;
        int res = INT_MIN;
        int n = nums.size();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            pre *= nums[i];
            suf *= nums[n - 1 - i];
            res = max({res, pre, suf});
            if (pre == 0) pre = 1;
            if (suf == 0) suf = 1;
        }

        return res;
    }
};
```

